00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:06.299
Speaker 1: We start today with the beginning
of the Dominion voting systems, Fox News defamation

00:00:06.299 --> 00:00:07.299
trial.

00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:11.930
This is a trial that could have such far ranging
impact, and we're going to be watching it

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.150
extraordinarily closely.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:16.580
Now, the trial was originally scheduled to
start yesterday.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:21.140
There was the announcement that there would
be a delay and there was the suspicion that

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:26.830
the delay might be because Fox News wanted
to settle the case and prevent it from going

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.010
to trial.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:34.030
Whether or not that's what the cause of the
delay was, the case is not being settled and

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.360
the trial is set to start today.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:42.110
CNBC reports Fox News and Dominion trial kicks
off with opening statements in defamation

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:43.670
suit.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:49.440
Dominion has accused Fox of intentionally
and falsely blaming it for President Donald

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:55.969
Trump's loss to Joe Biden by airing false
claims that the company rigged the 2020 election.

00:00:55.969 --> 00:01:00.820
Fox has maintained the statements made about
dominion on air are protected by the First

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:01.820
Amendment.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:06.500
The case has led to the release of troves
of private messages and testimony from top

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.590
Fox News figures, including Fox Corporation
Chairman Rupert Murdoch and opinion host Tucker

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:12.590
Carlson.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:17.409
So is a couple different things here that
are of absolutely critical importance.

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:24.659
First of all, the mere fact that Fox News
is asserting First Amendment protection isn't

00:01:24.659 --> 00:01:30.310
unique, and it's really important to understand
that there are many circumstances in which

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:32.799
there is defamation alleged.

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:36.079
And as a defense, the First Amendment is given.

00:01:36.079 --> 00:01:38.399
That doesn't make this case special.

00:01:38.399 --> 00:01:42.710
It doesn't particularly make it about actually
factual free speech.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:49.869
This is a case in which you are alleging defamation,
meaning incorrect claims knowingly made which

00:01:49.869 --> 00:01:55.350
are harmful to the reputation in this case
of dominion with the counter point that you

00:01:55.350 --> 00:02:03.990
can always issue as a defense to defamation
the truth of the claims made if it were true

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:10.590
that Trump won in 2020, but because of a rigging
done involving Dominion voting systems, Joe

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:11.980
Biden became president.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:16.200
If you could demonstrate that, then it would
by definition not be defamation.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.060
And we're going to get back to that in a moment.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:25.610
We are going to see, among other things, likely
even more documents and text messages and

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:26.790
communications come out.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:31.020
These are the very communications through
which we learned that there are some true

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:35.590
believers on Fox News staff, including people
like Maria BARTIROMO, that there are people

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:39.620
on Fox News staff like Tucker Carlson, who
despised Donald Trump passionately was the

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:44.140
word Tucker used to describe his hate for
Donald Trump.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:49.510
And on some level, this is sort of a lose
lose for Fox now that it's gotten to this

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:50.510
point.

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:54.860
And what I mean by that is if Fox were to
settle, they might avoid what now might be

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:59.890
4 to 6 weeks of disastrous headlines as more
evidence comes out in the trial.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:03.069
But they would be, to some degree, admitting
guilt.

00:03:03.069 --> 00:03:08.530
And the alternative is, well, you don't settle,
but you now have six weeks of potentially

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:13.150
disastrous headlines and at the end of it,
you still might lose a whole bunch of money

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:16.260
and your reputation could be irreparably damaged.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:21.980
Now, to get back to that, a defense to defamation
is proving the facts.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:26.480
Donald Trump's suggestion, which he posted
yesterday or the day before yesterday, we

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.890
talked about it yesterday, the truth, social
truth.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:29.890
Speaker 2: Central.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:34.380
Speaker 1: Was that Fox indeed do that and
say, hey, it's not defamation.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.700
Trump really won.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:41.709
Trump's idea posted on troth central in all
capital letters was quote, If Fox would finally

00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:47.240
admit that there was large scale cheating
and irregularities in the 2020 presidential

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:51.379
election, which would be a good thing for
them and for America, the case against them,

00:03:51.379 --> 00:03:55.400
which should not have existed at all, would
be greatly weakened.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.250
Backup those patriots at Fox instead of throwing
them under the bus.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.280
And they are right.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:05.379
There is so much proof like mass ballot stuffing
caught on government cameras, FBI colluding

00:04:05.379 --> 00:04:08.659
with Twitter and Facebook, state legislatures
not used, etc..

00:04:08.659 --> 00:04:11.470
Now, there's a couple interesting things about
this.

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:17.959
First of all, as I mentioned, defamation is
a legal term, false statements harmful to

00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:19.340
someone's reputation.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:21.190
Someone accuses you of defamation.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:24.440
One defense is prove that what you said is
true.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:29.340
The problem with Trump's idea, other than
the fact that Trump didn't win the November

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:33.990
of 2020 election and so you can't prove something
that's not true.

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:41.130
This particular case is narrowly focused on
the allegedly defamatory statements made about

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.240
Dominion voting systems involvement.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:50.620
Many of the things Trump is talking about
here ballot stuffing, FBI colluding with Twitter.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:57.720
Even if Fox tried to prove that in this trial,
it wouldn't be a useful defense because the

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:58.830
allegations in.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:06.080
Question that are allegedly defamatory are
the ones about Dominion voting systems specifically.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.550
Imagine the circus that that would be, though.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:15.410
Fox News didn't defame anyone because Trump
did win and Dominion voting Systems did do

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:18.930
whatever Mike Pillow says that they did with
the machines.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:23.240
Like imagine the circus that that would become
side story here.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:26.380
That's an important story that I do want to
mention as well.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:32.530
Angelo Carusone from Media Matters, who we've
interviewed on the program, he has a really

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:38.440
